# services/github-service/.env — never committed; chmod 600. Read by the token-injecting proxy (Caddy).
#
# A fine-grained GitHub personal access token (Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens):
#   - a PUBLIC config repo:  Repository access = "Public repositories (read-only)"; no repository permissions.
#   - a PRIVATE config repo: Resource owner = the repo's owner; Repository access = "Only select repositories" → that repo;
#                            Repository permissions: Contents = Read-only (Metadata read-only is added automatically).
# Any token can still read every public repo — the platform pin (GIT_FILE_SOURCE_PIN in the hub's .env) is the boundary:
# docs/SELF-HOST-KEPT-FILES.md ("Reading kept files from Git").
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=github_pat_REPLACE_ME

